  "scope": "A versioned, fixed-record schema and committed owner-bound runtime-to-gem5 daemon lifecycle. CP25 proves the bit-8 control contract, CP26 proves one exact bit-9 gpuReadWrite execution fixture, and CP27 adds the first direct OpenCL executable. CP28 accepts one ordinary Python Triton correctness entry through the normal external-backend driver, JIT, and launcher: the exact pure-b010 float32 add_kernel executes twice in one managed session with observed queue/signal/packet/allocation reuse, bit-exact output, and zero fallback. Reuse of the kernel source packet is inferred from stable identifiers because the trace exposes no kernel mapping ID. This remains one exact contiguous vecadd operator; it does not prove arbitrary Triton kernels, model operators, a final repository-local Triton prefix, multi-token inference, TP, CCL, generic gfx950/arbitrary HSACO, or performance.",
